{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01403",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.35,
      "end_seconds": 5.67,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "hi, doctor, I hope I'm not disturbing you"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.57,
      "end_seconds": 12.31,
      "duration_seconds": 4.74,
      "text": "Yes, come in and sit down. What brings you here today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 12.9,
      "end_seconds": 16.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "Well doctor thank you for seeing us."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 17.11,
      "end_seconds": 24.73,
      "duration_seconds": 7.62,
      "text": "well, I've been having being thirsty. I did try to ignore it for a while"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.6,
      "end_seconds": 33.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "What's the the timeline, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 35.19,
      "end_seconds": 42.79,
      "duration_seconds": 7.6,
      "text": "okay, uh, so probably about two weeks. Yeah. I told my wife I'd come today"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 43.53,
      "end_seconds": 46.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "how much trouble does it give you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 47.73,
      "end_seconds": 71.83,
      "duration_seconds": 24.1,
      "text": "It feels mild to me. As for tingling in my toes, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before. With tingling in my toes, I'd say mild. It happens on and off. Recurrent thrush was there, but it's gone away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.89,
      "end_seconds": 86.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "let me take your readings now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.46,
      "end_seconds": 95.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Nearly done with the the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.67,
      "end_seconds": 120.79,
      "duration_seconds": 10.12,
      "text": "Okay: BP is 172 over 93 weight 54 kilos height 151 centimetres. And temp 36.5 degrees pulse 89 BMI works out to 23.7."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.54,
      "end_seconds": 125.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "may I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.33,
      "end_seconds": 130.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "stay as you are for a moment"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 144.38,
      "end_seconds": 151.34,
      "duration_seconds": 6.96,
      "text": "the feeling at the tips of your toes is reduced and the foot pulses are present"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 156.86,
      "end_seconds": 159.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Okay, that's enough for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.89,
      "end_seconds": 182.02,
      "duration_seconds": 5.13,
      "text": "alright, any chest pain, foot ulcers or vomiting at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 183.29,
      "end_seconds": 188.01,
      "duration_seconds": 4.72,
      "text": "I haven't had chest pain, foot ulcers or vomiting, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.04,
      "end_seconds": 192.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "is your chest okay generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.87,
      "end_seconds": 195.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "no, nothing there"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.35,
      "end_seconds": 207.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "What operations have you had if any?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 209.41,
      "end_seconds": 227.55,
      "duration_seconds": 18.14,
      "text": "Okay, so I had my tonsils removed as a teenager. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.76,
      "end_seconds": 232.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "What conditions have you been treated for in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 236.59,
      "end_seconds": 241.01,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "High blood pressure, for five years. I've got diabetes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.87,
      "end_seconds": 248.96,
      "duration_seconds": 7.09,
      "text": "Yes. Alright, high blood pressure and diabetes, that matches what I have here. What's your work?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 250.67,
      "end_seconds": 254.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.06,
      "end_seconds": 257.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "Who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 258.77,
      "end_seconds": 261.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.74,
      "end_seconds": 264.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "do you follow any particular diet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 265.85,
      "end_seconds": 269.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "I'm vegetarian and have been for years"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.56,
      "end_seconds": 276.77,
      "duration_seconds": 6.21,
      "text": "right has anything ever caused you a a reaction? I mean any allergies"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 277.34,
      "end_seconds": 280.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "No I've never reacted to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 281.92,
      "end_seconds": 288.23,
      "duration_seconds": 6.31,
      "text": "Hold on, doctor, I think she reacted to diclofenac once. I'm not certain, though."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 289.59,
      "end_seconds": 292.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "Really? I don't think so."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 294.15,
      "end_seconds": 300.43,
      "duration_seconds": 6.28,
      "text": "fair enough I'll write down both versions are you taking anything regularly including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 300.94,
      "end_seconds": 316.8,
      "duration_seconds": 15.86,
      "text": "She is on ramipril, 5 milligrams, every morning for my blood pressure, I give it to to her. She takes Glycomet, 500 milligrams, twice a day for my sugar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 318.6,
      "end_seconds": 328.6,
      "duration_seconds": 10.0,
      "text": "so where does that leave us? This is probably diabetes not well controlled on current treatment. Early nerve damage is also on my list"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 329.61,
      "end_seconds": 332.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "oh, will it clear up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 333.61,
      "end_seconds": 354.31,
      "duration_seconds": 20.7,
      "text": "nothing I've seen today points to an emergency it looks like diabetes not well controlled on current treatment but I'd like to confirm let me just check I've got this right you've had being thirsty for about two weeks mild and no chest pain or vomiting"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 355.7,
      "end_seconds": 356.4,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "correct"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 357.97,
      "end_seconds": 381.98,
      "duration_seconds": 24.01,
      "text": "let's get a urine albumin test, for diabetes review we should do an HbA1c for diabetes review i'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more what I'm giving you is gliclazide, 40 milligrams, once a day with breakfast, long term you take it by mouth that should help with diabetes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 382.96,
      "end_seconds": 386.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "is that safe with my other medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 388.6,
      "end_seconds": 404.35,
      "duration_seconds": 15.75,
      "text": "check your feet daily and book the eye screening try to keep a simple diary of when it happens and what you were doing, and bring it to the next visit i think the diabetes educator should see you too"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 409.5,
      "end_seconds": 410.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "Alright, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 412.0,
      "end_seconds": 417.61,
      "duration_seconds": 5.61,
      "text": "Let's plan a a check in three months. Have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 422.05,
      "end_seconds": 425.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "I think I understand everything. Thanks."
    }
  ]
}